# Nothing here is required to replay an already-recorded artifact -- replay
# makes no model call of any kind. Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored,
# never committed) only if you need one of the cases below.

# Lets discovery drive decisions over the raw Anthropic API (--backend
# anthropic) instead of the `claude` CLI (--backend claude-cli, which needs
# no key -- just the CLI already logged in). Unset by default; with no key
# and no backend flag, discovery falls back to a local Ollama model instead
# of failing.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Where the Ollama backend sends requests (--backend ollama, or --backend
# auto with no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). Same variable the `ollama` CLI reads, so
# if you already point that at a remote GPU box, this picks it up too.
# `--ollama-host` on the command line overrides it. Default: localhost:11434.
# OLLAMA_HOST=

# Comma-separated extra env var names to treat as secrets during recording,
# beyond what's already detected by name (*PASSWORD*, *TOKEN*, *SECRET*,
# *API_KEY*). Only matters when recording a capability against a target
# whose login needs a real credential that isn't shaped like one of those --
# e.g. a username/email that's sensitive without being credential-shaped by
# name.
# AGENT_CREDENTIAL_VARS=

# Any credential named above (or auto-detected by name) is referenced by a
# recorded artifact only as {{env:VAR_NAME}} -- never as a literal -- and is
# resolved from whatever process's environment replays it. If you record a
# capability that needs one, define it here with that same name, e.g.:
# MY_TARGET_PASSWORD=
